"The :mod:`subprocess` module now uses the :func:`~os.posix_spawn` function "
"in more situations, including when *close_fds* is ``True`` (the default) on "
"many modern platforms. This should provide a notable performance increase "
"when launching processes on FreeBSD and Solaris. See the :ref:`subprocess "
"<whatsnew313-subprocess>` section above for details. (Contributed by Jakub "
"Kulik in :gh:`113117`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`subprocess` nyni pouziva funkci :func:`~os.posix_spawn` ve vice "
"situacich, vcinetne kdy je *close_fds* ``True`` (vychozi) na mnoha modernich"
" platformach. To by melo poskytnout vyznamne zlepseni vykonu pri spousteni "
"procesu na FreeBSD a Solarisu. Detaily najdete v casti :ref:`subprocess "
"<whatsnew313-subprocess>` vyse. (Prispeno Jakub Kulik v :gh:`113117`.)"

