#: ../../whatsnew/3.13.rst:2269
msgid "Changed C APIs"
msgstr "Zmeny C API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.13.rst:2271
msgid ""
"The *keywords* parameter of :c:func:`PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords` and "
":c:func:`PyArg_VaParseTupleAndKeywords` now has type :c:expr:`char * const "
"*` in C and :c:expr:`const char * const *` in C++, instead of :c:expr:`char "
"**`. In C++, this makes these functions compatible with arguments of type "
":c:expr:`const char * const *`, :c:expr:`const char **`, or :c:expr:`char * "
"const *` without an explicit type cast. In C, the functions only support "
"arguments of type :c:expr:`char * const *`. This can be overridden with the "
":c:macro:`PY_CXX_CONST` macro. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":gh:`65210`.)"
msgstr ""
"Parametr *keywords* funkci :c:func:`PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords` a "
":c:func:`PyArg_VaParseTupleAndKeywords` ma nyni typ :c:expr:`char * const *`"
" v C a :c:expr:`const char * const *` v C++, namiste :c:expr:`char **`. V "
"C++ to cinilo tyto funkce kompatibilni s argumenty typu :c:expr:`const char "
"* const *`, :c:expr:`const char **` nebo :c:expr:`char * const *` bez "
"explicitniho pretypovani. V C funkce podporuji pouze argumenty typu "
":c:expr:`char * const *`. To lze pretezit makrem :c:macro:`PY_CXX_CONST`. "
"(Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :gh:`65210`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.13.rst:2283
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords` now supports non-ASCII keyword "
"parameter names. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :gh:`110815`.)"
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords` nyni podporuje ASCII parametry "
"klicovych slov. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :gh:`110815`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.13.rst:2287
msgid ""
"The :c:func:`!PyCode_GetFirstFree` function is now unstable API and is now "
"named :c:func:`PyUnstable_Code_GetFirstFree`. (Contributed by Bogdan "
"Romanyuk in :gh:`115781`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :c:func:`!PyCode_GetFirstFree` je nyni nestabilni API a je nyni "
"pojmenovana :c:func:`PyUnstable_Code_GetFirstFree`. (Prispel Bogdan Romanyuk"
" v :gh:`115781`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.13.rst:2291
msgid ""
"The :c:func:`PyDict_GetItem`, :c:func:`PyDict_GetItemString`, "
":c:func:`PyMapping_HasKey`, :c:func:`PyMapping_HasKeyString`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_HasAttr`, :c:func:`PyObject_HasAttrString`, and "
":c:func:`PySys_GetObject` functions, each of which clears all errors which "
"occurred when calling them now reports these errors using "
":func:`sys.unraisablehook`. You may replace them with other functions as "
"recommended in the documentation. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":gh:`106672`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :c:func:`PyDict_GetItem`, :c:func:`PyDict_GetItemString`, "
":c:func:`PyMapping_HasKey`, :c:func:`PyMapping_HasKeyString`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_HasAttr`, :c:func:`PyObject_HasAttrString` a "
":c:func:`PySys_GetObject`, z nichz kazda zmazava vsechny chyby, ktere se "
"vyskytyly pri jejich volani, nyni hlasi tyto chyby pouzitim "
":func:`sys.unraisablehook`. Muzes je nahradit jinymi funkcemi, jak je "
"doporuceno v dokumentaci. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :gh:`106672`.)"

